    use: ["List the variable cells exactly, and don't include formula cells.", "Each limit is one row in the solver window.", "Change the sheet without updating the cell ranges and you are solving a different problem."],
    precise: "A variable cell has to be a number the solver is allowed to change. Point at a formula cell by mistake and you either get an error, or you think you are choosing something a formula is already holding. Declare linearity while the model has an IF or a product of two variables and the sensitivity report no longer means what it says. Keep the model in a small range you can read, the same way a macro is not allowed to hide a decision.",
